<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 28 March, from 193 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">193</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Praetorians murder Pertinax and auction the empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After killing Emperor Pertinax, the Praetorian Guard sold the throne to the senator Didius Julianus, who outbid his rival. He lasted 66 days before Septimius Severus took power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1854</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France declare war on Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The two powers joined the Ottoman Empire against Russia, beginning their part in the Crimean War. Battlefield reporting and Florence Nightingale's nursing made it a turning point in public views of war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1910</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henri Fabre makes the first seaplane flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The French engineer took off from the Étang de Berre near Marseille in his float-equipped Hydravion. It was the first powered aircraft to take off from water.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1941</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Virginia Woolf drowns herself in the River Ouse</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fearing a return of mental illness, the novelist filled her pockets with stones and walked into the river near her Sussex home. Her novels include 'Mrs Dalloway' and 'To the Lighthouse'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1979</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Partial meltdown at Three Mile Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A cooling failure caused part of a reactor core to melt at the Pennsylvania nuclear plant. Little radiation escaped, but it was the worst US nuclear accident and stalled new reactor orders.</p></li></ol>
